WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.800
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:13.080
These amazing images were all made by an AI&nbsp;
called DALL-E 2. This AI is endowed with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:18.840
diffusion-based model, which means that when&nbsp;
we ask it something, it starts out from noise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:26.760
and over time, it iteratively refines this image&nbsp;
to match our description better. And, over time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:35.100
magically, an absolutely incredible image emerges.&nbsp;
This is a neural network that is given a ton of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:42.900
images, and a piece of text that says what is&nbsp;
in this image. That is one image-caption pair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:50.940
DALL-E 2 is given millions and millions of these&nbsp;
pairs. So, what can it do with all this knowledge?

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:58.560
The key takeaway here is that it does no, or&nbsp;
very little copying from this training data, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:06.420
it truly comes up with novel images. How? Well,&nbsp;
after it had seen a bunch of images of koalas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:14.160
and separately, a bunch of images of motorcycles,&nbsp;
it starts to understand the concept of both,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:20.100
and it will be able to combine the two&nbsp;
together into a completely new image.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:24.540
And luckily, due to the generosity of OpenAI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:29.460
I also have access and I tried&nbsp;
my best to push it to its limits.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.700
It can also generate an image of you&nbsp;
Fellow Scholars marveling at this paper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:42.960
or in the process of reading an even&nbsp;
more explosive paper. So good! I also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:48.240
tried this fox scientist in an earlier&nbsp;
episode, and it came out extremely well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:54.960
with tons of personality. And, hold on to&nbsp;
your papers because due to popular request,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.960 --> 00:02:01.020
you are getting some more variants from&nbsp;
my experiment with it. And DALL-E 2 did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:05.940
not disappoint. This character can&nbsp;
be recreated as a beautiful sculpture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:13.980
with several amazing variants, Dragonball&nbsp;
style, and it is also a true merch monster.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:22.740
But, we also tested it against the works of real&nbsp;
artists. My opinion is that it is not yet as good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:30.360
as a world-class artist, here are some tests&nbsp;
against Judit Somogyvári’s work, and it is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:39.600
not as good as the king of donuts, Andrew Price,&nbsp;
however, DALL-E 2 is able to create 10,000 images&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:48.120
every day. That is a different kind of value&nbsp;
proposition. So, we ask today, after these amazing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:55.020
results, does it really have more surprises up&nbsp;
the sleeve? Oh boy. By the end of this video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.020 --> 00:03:01.320
you will see how much of a silly question that&nbsp;
is. So today, we are going to have a look at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:08.460
10 recent amazing results, some of which are from&nbsp;
prompts that I ran for you on Twitter. Let’s see!

